===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|hemlok|lang=enm}}, {{term|hemeluc|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|hymlīc}}, {{term/t|ang|hymlīce||hemlock, bryony, convulvus}}, literally 'hops-like', from {{term|hymele||hop-vine|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*humalaz}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*humalōn}}, of unknown origin. Perhaps from {{etyl|xsc|en}} {{term/t|xsc|*haumala}}, a diminutive of {{term/t|xsc|*hauma||ephedra; juice}}, from {{etyl|iir-pro|en}} {{term/t|iir-pro|*sauma}} from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*seue-||to suck; juice}}.

{{rel-top|cognates}}
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Germanic *humalaz, *humalōn}} {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|humall|lang=non}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|homele|lang=gml}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *haumala}} [[Ossetian]] {{term|хумæллæг|tr=xumællæg||hops|lang=os}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *hauma}} {{etyl|ae|-}} {{term|tr=haoma|lang=ae}}{{rfscript|ae}}, [[Baluchi]] {{term|tr=hum|lang=bal}}{{rfscript|und|sc=Arab}}, {{etyl|fa|-}} {{term|هوم|tr=hōm|lang=fa}})
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Indo-Iranian *sauma}} [[Sanskrit]] {{term|सोम|tr=soma|lang=sa}})
More at [[suck]].
{{rel-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[coniferous]] [[tree]]s, of the genus ''[[Tsuga]]'', that grow in [[North America]]; the [[wood]] of such trees.
# A [[poisonous]] [[umbellifer]]ous [[plant]]s, of the genera ''[[Conium]]'', either ''[[Conium maculatum]]'' or {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}.
# The [[water hemlock]] plant, genus ''[[Cicuta]]''.
# The [[poison]] obtained from these plants.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|''Conium''}} [[beaver poison]], [[devil's porridge]], [[Herb Bennet]], [[musquash root]], [[poison hemlock]], [[poison parsley]], [[spotted corobane]], [[spotted hemlock]] ''[[Conium maculatum]]''; {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}; {{taxlink|Conium conium maculatum|subspecies}}

